---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use for Melveo. Clubs pay, players never."
  lang="en"
>
  <PageHeader lang="en" />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent-primary)]">
      Placeholder version · 2026-04-30
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-balance text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Terms of use
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      Provisional. Binding text becomes effective before the first paid
      licence.
    </p>

    <hr class="my-12 border-[var(--color-stroke-base)]" />

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Operator</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      <strong>QUIX Global s.r.o.</strong>, IČO 22466444, registered office:
      Příčná 1892/4, 110 00 Prague 1, Czech Republic; Commercial Register
      kept by the Municipal Court in Prague, section C, file 416432. Data
      box: <code>g7v78rx</code>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Licensing model</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      <strong>1 licence = 1 team × 1 season.</strong> The payer is always
      the club (legal entity or statutory representative). Players and
      coaches never pay for the app directly — access is granted via
      club invitation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Payments</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      Payments are processed by Stripe Inc. Card or invoice accepted.
      The iOS app is a <em>companion app</em> per Apple App Store
      §3.1.3(f) — all commerce happens on the web, never in iOS.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Liability &amp; limitations</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      <li>
        Melveo is not a medical device. Wellness check-ins serve sports
        training, not medical decisions.
      </li>
      <li>
        The club is responsible for ensuring player consent (incl. minors
        via legal guardian).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-stroke-emphasized)] bg-[var(--color-bg-surface)] p-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      <strong>Dev note:</strong> final terms will be added in V4-B, including
      jurisdiction, dispute resolution, and operator details after legal
      review.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
